---
import PolicyPage from '../components/common/PolicyPage.astro';
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What FateTide stores and what it does not: no accounts or questions collected, a daily card kept only in your browser, what is in share links, hosting logs, Cloudflare Web Analytics, and advertising."
  path="/privacy/"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  lead="FateTide is built to need as little personal information as possible. This page describes what the site does today, and what would change if advertising is added."
  updated
>
  <section aria-labelledby="summary-title">
    <h2 id="summary-title">In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There are no accounts, forms, or comment sections, and FateTide does not ask for your name, email, birth details, or questions.</li>
      <li>Your card of the day is kept in your own browser and is not sent to FateTide.</li>
      <li>Page views are counted in aggregate with Cloudflare Web Analytics, without your readings or anything you typed.</li>
      <li>Advertising is not enabled at the moment. This policy will be updated when advertising is enabled.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="collect-title">
    <h2 id="collect-title">Information FateTide does not collect</h2>
    <p>The site does not include any way to type a question or personal details, so nothing like that is saved, sent, or shared. Tarot draws happen in your browser and are not stored on a server. FateTide does not use accounts and does not set its own cookies.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="device-title">
    <h2 id="device-title">Stored on your device</h2>
    <p>The Today's Fortune page saves your card of the day in your browser's local storage, using one entry that holds the card, whether it is upright or reversed, and the date. It stays on your device, it is what lets a reload show the same card, and it is replaced when the date changes. You can remove it at any time by clearing this site's data in your browser settings.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="links-title">
    <h2 id="links-title">Information in links</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Horoscope:</strong> choosing a sign adds it to the page address after a # sign. Browsers do not send that part of an address to the website.</li>
      <li><strong>Compatibility:</strong> the two signs you choose are added to the address as a query, so you can bookmark or share the result.</li>
      <li><strong>Shared tarot readings:</strong> a share link contains the reading type, card identifiers, whether each card is upright or reversed, the focus for One Card and Three Card, and the date for a daily card. It contains nothing you typed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you share a link, the people and apps you send it to can see that content, and it may appear in your browser history. Shared reading pages ask search engines not to list them.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="hosting-title">
    <h2 id="hosting-title">Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>FateTide is a static website delivered by a hosting provider. Like almost any website, the provider processes basic technical information, such as your IP address, the address you requested, and your browser type, in order to deliver the site and keep it secure. FateTide does not combine this information with any account or profile, because none exists.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="analytics-title">
    <h2 id="analytics-title">Analytics</h2>
    <p>FateTide uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to see, in aggregate, which pages are visited and how quickly they load. Cloudflare describes it as privacy-focused and as measuring page views and performance without using cookies to track individual visitors. It receives basic technical information such as the page address and your browser type. FateTide does not send it your readings or anything you typed, and the site runs no other analytics. If that changes, this page will be updated.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ads-title">
    <h2 id="ads-title">Advertising</h2>
    <p>Advertising is not currently enabled, and no advertising code runs on the site. If advertising is enabled later, it may be provided by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may then use cookies, local storage, or similar technologies to show and measure ads, including personalized ads where the law and your choices allow. In regions where consent is required, a consent message from Google or a Google-certified consent management platform would be shown before such ads. You can read how Google uses information from sites that use its services at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>. This policy will be updated when advertising is enabled.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="children-title">
    <h2 id="children-title">Children</h2>
    <p>FateTide is not directed to children under 13, and it does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="choices-title">
    <h2 id="choices-title">Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can clear this site's stored data, block cookies and local storage, or use private browsing at any time through your browser settings. FateTide's readings work without any account.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="changes-title">
    <h2 id="changes-title">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We will update this page when the way the site handles information changes, and the date at the top will change with it.</p>
  </section>
</PolicyPage>
